+
+### Phase 21: Bilingual (RU <-> EN) Technical Terminology Mapper, Page Security Posture Inspector & Contradiction Resolution Audit Matrix Builder
+- **`desktop/windows/browser/bilingual-terminology-mapper.cjs`**:
+  - `resolveCanonicalCriterion(rawLabel)` and `alignBilingualClaimsForOption(optionName, claims)`: normalizes bilingual Russian and English criterion headers (`"Месячная стоимость"` / `"Monthly Price"`, `"SLA аптайма"` / `"Uptime SLA"`, `"Задержка p95"` / `"p95 Latency"`, `"Лимит ОЗУ"` / `"RAM Limit"`, `"Шифрование"` / `"Encryption"`, `"Регион ЦОД"` / `"Data Center Region"`, `"Экспорт данных"` / `"Data Export"`, `"Ролевой доступ"` / `"RBAC / SSO"`) and bilingual unit expressions (`"$49/мес"` vs `"49 USD/month"`, `"64 ГБ"` vs `"65536 MB"`, `"< 12 мс"` vs `"0.012 sec"`) so cross-language sources corroborate or surface contradictions without false negatives.
+- **`desktop/windows/browser/page-security-posture-inspector.cjs`**:
+  - `inspectPageSecurityPosture({ url, statusCode, headers, html })`: audits transport scheme (`https:` vs `http:` vs `synthetic:`), security headers (`Strict-Transport-Security`, `Content-Security-Policy`, `X-Frame-Options`, `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`), mixed-content form action URLs (`http://` form submission targets on `https://` pages), and untrusted third-party `<script src="...">` inclusions.
+- **`desktop/windows/browser/contradiction-resolution-matrix.cjs`**:
+  - `buildContradictionResolutionMatrix(claims)`, `renderContradictionMatrixMarkdown(matrix)`, and `saveContradictionResolutionMatrixViaWorkspace({ workspaceRoot, slug, claims })`: groups competing claims per `(optionName, criterion)`, applies temporal precedence (`eventDate > pageDate > fetchedAt`) via `compareFactsForCriterion`, and saves a dedicated side-by-side Markdown (`reports/<slug>.md`) and JSON (`reports/<slug>.json`) Contradiction Resolution Audit Matrix with exact UTF-16 `[startUtf16..endUtf16]` excerpts via `workspace-service.cjs`.
+- **Exposed via `shell.cjs` (`browser.align_bilingual_claims`, `browser.inspect_page_security`, `browser.build_contradiction_matrix`) and verified in Subtests 34 and 35 (`45/45` total suites passing).**
